  "chain": "unclear vendor/procedural guidance on plastic guide orientation [cause D] -> plunger well plastic guides incorrectly installed + upper guide bracket warped -> actuator binding -> solenoid burnout / ERV 3B fails to actuate -> ADS valve 2-0203-3B inoperable for entire cycle (no BACKED_UP_BY; four of five ADS valves credited, engineering evaluation found design/licensing bases still met)",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Not an SSFF per engineering evaluation (4-of-5 ADS valves credited in LOCA analysis); event is an MRFF. No BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted since the other ADS valves are described as design-basis redundancy for the ADS function, not a stated-operable backup system distinct from the ADS itself. Previous occurrence LER 265/2020-002-00 involved ERV 3D with a different root cause (out-of-spec plunger) despite similar bent/warped guide bracket contributing factor; captured as stub with key exactly as stated in narrative."
